# Cloudflare Pages Redirects
# Docs: https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/
#
# IMPORTANT: under @astrojs/cloudflare, paths route through dist/_worker.js
# and the static `_redirects` is bypassed for in-app paths. That's why we
# CANNOT define these as `redirects` in astro.config.mjs (only `/` works
# there because it's excluded from the worker via _routes.json).
#
# We DO get _redirects honored for paths the worker doesn't catch — and
# practically, Cloudflare Pages applies path-level rules at the edge for
# anything that 404s in the SPA. These cross-language 404 recoveries
# fall in that bucket: the source URLs don't exist as routes so the
# worker yields, and Cloudflare's _redirects then fires.
#
# Sources are taken from GSC Page Indexing → Not found (404), 2026-06-02.
# Only URLs Google actually has indexed are listed — no speculative coverage.

